window.EN={"1":"Ostia was known far and wide as the land of the \"Fierce General\" —","2":"it boasted an army built around armor knights and generals, heavy knights commanded by its lord, Hector.","3":"The Ostia Castle they guarded had never once let an enemy breach it in the past,","4":"and for hundreds of years had been spoken of as \"impregnable.\"","5":"But now, that history was about to come to an end —","6":"ironically, at the hands of Roy and his companions, who meant to protect Ostia...","7":"Wh-what did you say!? You're telling me the enemy's gotten inside the castle!?","8":"Damn it all, what was Dabhyss doing!?","9":"Are the Ilian knights stronger than I expected, or did more people side with them than I thought...?","10":"Either way, they've put a scratch on the history of this \"impregnable\" castle, curse them!","11":"What a disaster. If it comes to this, Bern will see us as weak.","12":"But there's no turning back now... f-for now, let's just suppress the unrest...","13":"Hey! Listen carefully.","14":"Sir!","15":"I won't let the enemy do as they please inside this castle.","16":"Whatever it takes, hold them back!","17":"Station soldiers throughout the castle — especially around this throne, thoroughly!","18":"Yes, sir!","19":"And as for Lilina — get rid of her quietly, under cover of the fighting!","20":"B-but... weren't we told to keep her alive?","21":"I meant to use her as leverage against them,","22":"but there are still plenty among our own men who are fond of that little girl.","23":"Using her openly as a hostage risks turning sympathy — and maybe even our own men — against us...","24":"B-but if we go so far as to kill her with our own hands, that's exactly the kind of thing that'll draw condemnation...","25":"That's why I said quietly, didn't I!","26":"Make it look like she was hit by a stray arrow from an archer, and pin the blame on the enemy!","27":"Now go, quickly!","28":"Y-yes sir...","29":"...You're General Roy of the Lycian Alliance, aren't you?","30":"! Who are you? An enemy!?","31":"I'm on your side. Relax.","32":"My name's Astore. I used to work under Lord Ostia.","33":"Forgive my rudeness, but what exactly was your line of work?","34":"You don't really look like someone who served the Marquess of Ostia...","35":"That's a rude thing to say, old man — though I get what you mean.","36":"Getting hold of enemy information, scouting out the state of cities...","37":"What you might call \"under-the-table work.\"","38":"Hmph. I see.","39":"If people could tell at a glance that I worked for some big shot, I couldn't do my job, see.","40":"For about the past month, I've been going around various regions gathering intelligence on Lord Ostia's orders.","41":"When I learned of the Marquess's death near Araphen, I rushed back here, only to find—","42":"that bastards Dabhyss and Reygans had gone and started a rebellion.","43":"I was too late for Lord Hector, but I want to save Lady Lilina somehow, if I can.","44":"We feel the same way. Let's join forces and get through this crisis.","45":"Mr. Astore, do you know where Lilina is being held?","46":"Of course. Finding things like that out is exactly my job.","47":"Lady Lilina's locked up in a small room in the center of the castle.","48":"And that traitor Reygans is lounging on his throne in the back.","49":"Alright, let's hurry.","50":"Before Bern's General Narcian arrives, we need to crush the rebels and save Lilina!","51":"This commotion... has fighting broken out inside the castle?","52":"I wonder what's happening outside...","53":"Huh? Mr. Bath.","54":"It's a dead end!","55":"Don't worry. There's a crack in the wall further in.","56":"Strike it a few times with a sword or lance and it should break.","57":"Lady Lilina... where could she be?","58":"I've got a rough idea.","59":"This is the castle we've always protected, after all.","60":"Still, it's awfully noisy over there.","61":"Is there fighting going on?","62":"Probably.","63":"Could be the Ilian mercenary knights attacking, or if we're lucky, survivors of the Alliance army...","64":"Survivors of the Alliance army? Then... my brother, too...?","65":"...Whether he himself survived or not, I can't say.","66":"It's better not to hold onto false hope.","67":"...Ah, yes.","68":"Mr. Oujay, that's a harsh thing to say.","69":"For Wendy, that's her one and only brother we're talking about, isn't it?","70":"There's no point looking away from reality.","71":"But still...","72":"It's alright, Oujay. Bath's just telling it straight.","73":"No matter what happens, don't lose your composure, as an Ostian knight... understand, Wendy?","74":"...Yes.","75":"Heh heh, just as I figured, they're at it again. Honestly, these high-and-mighty types are fools.","76":"What's so fun about fighting wars all the time?","77":"Ah, whatever. Since I'm here, might as well take what I can get!","78":"Ah!","79":"Fu, funny how often we keep running into each other, huh. Ha ha ha...","80":"...If you're only on this battlefield to steal things,","81":"I think you should stop. That's not a good thing to do.","82":"Relax, relax. I only go after the \"fine nobles,\" after all.","83":"Nobody's going to be left struggling to get by because of it.","84":"I don't think that's really the point...","85":"Hmm... then let me ask you something. What about you lot?","86":"Don't you take the crops people grow","87":"from the land you lot just decided was \"your territory,\" without asking them?","88":"Wha—! But in return, we protect people's lives and—","89":"You don't protect us! Not when you go starting wars like this!","90":"This is because the Kingdom of Bern attacked. We're protecting everyone from Bern, so—","91":"So it's fine to do anything as long as you say it's \"to protect\"? Even if it means burning villages or ruining fields?","92":"Burning villages... that's not something... ! Wait, could it be...","93":"...My village was burned down by its own lord.","94":"He said, \"Bern's coming, it's necessary for strategy,\" and that was that.","95":"Th-that's...","96":"We barely had enough to eat as it was, and we lost our home, our fields too... everyone scattered, apart...","97":"\"You mustn't take what belongs to others\"?","98":"Hmph! You lot, living comfortably off what you took from the people of the land—","99":"what right do you have to say that to my face!?","100":"I... I don't know what to say...","101":"Ahh, man, this got kind of heavy, didn't it.","102":"I don't really like talking about this stuff, you know... feels like bragging about \"poor little me\" or something.","103":"This only turned into this because you acted like you understood something.","104":"I... I'm just...","105":"Ugh, this got complicated, now it's hard to just walk away.","106":"Well, times like this, guess I should just wrap it up and head home.","107":"See ya, bye.","108":".........","109":"Brother! Thank goodness you're safe!!","110":"Oh, Wendy, is that you? Glad you're safe too!","111":"...!? Wh-what happened to you? What's with that outfit?","112":"Don't tell me... you joined the Ostia Heavy Knights...?","113":"...Yes. A few days ago, I took my knight's oath.","114":"What have you done...","115":"I told you before you left — leave the fighting to us, just think about your own happiness.","116":"Didn't I say that enough times!?","117":"Yes. Since then, I've thought it over a lot.","118":"But in the end, this is still the path I want to walk!","119":"But...","120":"I didn't want to just keep waiting for you to come back from the fighting forever.","121":"My happiness is becoming a splendid knight, one who won't lose to you.","122":".........","123":"...Brother?","124":"Honestly, you've never listened once you've made up your mind, ever since you were little.","125":"Brother...","126":"Go on and walk the path you believe in.","127":"If Father and Mother were still alive, I'm sure they'd have said the same.","128":"But the path you've chosen... it's a hard one, you know?","129":"Yes, I'm prepared for that! I absolutely won't lose!!","130":"Lilina!!","131":"Eh... Roy? Is it really you?","132":"Of course it's me, Lilina!","133":"Roy, you came! I'm so happy...","134":"Lilina, I'm so glad you're really safe. It's alright now!","135":"Here, take this tome for now, to protect yourself with.","136":"Thank you.","137":"L-Lady Lilina!! Thank goodness... you're safe!","138":"Bors, I'm sorry for worrying you.","139":"Not at all! You're alive... that's all that matters to me...","140":"That alone is enough, for this Bors...","141":"Thank you, Bors, for worrying about me.","142":"And more than that — you kept your promise and protected Roy.","143":"I knew I was right to ask you.","144":"Lady Lilina!!","145":"Bath!","146":"Lady Lilina! I'm so relieved you're safe.","147":"Bath, you were right.","148":"Reygans and the others were just waiting for the right moment to start their rebellion.","149":".........","150":"I'm sorry. If only I had trusted you...","151":"this wouldn't have happened...","152":"No.","153":"It's Reygans and the others who are to blame, for trampling on your kind feelings","154":"toward them, Lady Lilina — trying to trust them.","155":"You have nothing to apologize for, Lady Lilina.","156":"It's exactly that kindness of yours that all of us have always admired.","157":"Bath...","158":"Bors — so you're alive, are you.","159":"Of course.","160":"...While we were away, you had the nerve to do this to Ostia!","161":"If you have a complaint, try taking it back —","162":"with that arm of yours!","163":"Lady Lilina... tch, so you botched it.","164":"Reygans, why...?","165":"The times are changing, that's all. I'm simply following that tide.","166":"Unlike that foolish Lord Hector, who couldn't read it.","167":"Silence! I won't allow you to speak ill of my father!","168":"Lord Reygans — prepare yourself!","169":"Hoh, you're... Bors's, I believe...","170":"Brave words, but can this old man take you down? Heh heh heh.","171":"Reygans, you—","172":"Betraying your own house — aren't you ashamed of yourself!?","173":"Bath, is it...","174":"Hmph, better than going down together with a foolish lord.","175":"What did you say! Reygans, you've rotted that far, have you!!","176":"Insufferable, you half-dead remnants of that Alliance...","177":"Come, then. I'll cut down every last one of you!","178":"Why...?","179":"You lot, who should've been crushed by Bern...","180":"why can you still fight this hard...?","181":"(if Lilina survives)","182":"Lilina, we finally got the castle back.","183":"Thank you, it's all thanks to Roy and everyone else.","184":"I'm glad — this way Father won't have to trouble himself over it.","185":"!","186":"Hey, Roy, is Father still at Araphen?","187":"I heard the fighting there was very fierce — is it dragging on?","188":"Lilina... hasn't anyone told you anything?","189":"Eh? Told me what?","190":"...Please listen calmly. Lord Hector... has passed away.","191":"Eh...?","192":"I'm sorry. By the time we reached Araphen,","193":"the castle was already under Bern's control...","194":"...It's not your fault, Roy... don't apologize.","195":"Lord Hector was already... gravely wounded by then.","196":"If we'd arrived just a little sooner... we might have saved him... it's my own lack of strength.","197":"D-don't worry about it... I-I was prepared for this...","198":"Yeah... I was prepared...........","199":"I'm the daughter of a warrior. I was raised to not lose my composure, especially at times like this.","200":"Lilina.","201":"So, all of you, you don't have to hide things from me — it's alright to tell me right away.","202":"Everyone's being too considerate with me... I'm... actually pretty strong, you know...","203":"Lilina, you don't have to force yourself, not in front of me.","204":"Roy... I... I...","205":"I'm right here beside you.","206":"(if Lilina died)","207":"Lord Roy, this is terrible! Bern's wyvern knights are outside Ostia Castle!","208":"What!? They're already here?","209":"Heh heh heh. You're the one called Roy, I take it?","210":"Much appreciated, taking down those fools Reygans and his lot for me — saved me some trouble.","211":"Now then, be good and hand Ostia over to us.","212":"You've got to be joking! Who'd ever hand it over to the likes of you...!!","213":"Oh, so you'd rather fight us? With that battered-up force of yours?","214":"Interesting. Then let me crush you thoroughly — just like I did with Hector, Marquess of Ostia.","215":"Agh!","216":"(off-screen) That's far enough!","217":"G-General Narcian! A huge force from the Kingdom of Etruria!","218":"Argh, I can see that much just by looking! Just why on earth...","219":"I am Percival, General of the Knights of the Kingdom of Etruria.","220":"A few days ago, through Cecilia, our General of Magic, a request for protection was made from Ostia to our nation.","221":"Accordingly, Ostia now falls under the protection of the Kingdom of Etruria.","222":"Wh-what...","223":"Dissatisfied? Then we're willing to cross swords with you, if you insist.","224":"Though I wonder — can those dragon knights of yours really handle this many of us, impressive as they look?","225":"Y-you are...","226":"I am Cecilia, General of Magic of the Kingdom of Etruria.","227":"This Ostia has ties to me. I won't let you have your way with it.","228":"Guh... damn it... damn you!","229":"General Narcian, don't let your temper get the better of you!","230":"General Percival is one of Etruria's finest commanders.","231":"And with the magic corps joining in, fighting with dragon knights alone puts us at a disadvantage...","232":"I know that much!! Fall back!!","233":"Cecilia, was it? Insolent woman, I'll remember you!","234":"Are you General Roy of the Lycian Alliance?","235":"Y-yes, sir!","236":"I've been entrusted with an army by the late Lord of Ostia.","237":"I see. Lycia faces a trial, then. I've also been charged by my king of Etruria","238":"to convey his condolences for the Marquess's death.","239":"I'm grateful for Your Majesty's concern.","240":"Without Etruria's assistance...","241":"Ostia would likely have fallen under Bern's rule by now.","242":"Thank you, truly, from the bottom of my heart.","243":"It's not me you should be thanking — I merely followed my country's decision.","244":"If you want to thank someone, thank the General of Magic, who pushed back against a reluctant king.","245":"You... defied your king?","246":"That's right. Reckless of me, wasn't it?","247":"Now then, it wouldn't do for two generals to be away from our country for too long.","248":"I'll take my leave here.","249":"Cecilia!","250":"I'll leave the rest to you.","251":"Yes, leave it to me.","252":"Phew... General Percival... what presence.","253":"Heh heh heh... seems you were tense.","254":"Cecilia! It's been a while.","255":"You look a little tired, but otherwise well, Roy.","256":"Yes, thanks to the Etrurian army, we managed to avoid disaster.","257":"I'm glad we made it in time.","258":"Sorry... it seems we put you to a lot of trouble...","259":"No, that's not it at all.","260":"Your request for Ostia's protection was something that benefited Etruria too.","261":"Benefited...you?","262":"Yes, that's right.","263":"Bern's recent actions have been getting out of hand, haven't they?","264":"Our country wanted to do something about it too, but we hadn't been directly attacked ourselves...","265":"But if Bern grows any more powerful than this, the balance of power will be thrown off.","266":"And that's when Ostia's request came in, is that it?","267":"That's right.","268":"We simply judged it the right thing to do and acted on it — you don't need to feel indebted, Roy.","269":"I understand.","270":"So there's no need to thank us.","271":"Yes, I won't say it, then.","272":"For now, please come inside. Come meet everyone in the army.","273":"Heh... in the short time I haven't seen you, you've grown quite a bit sturdier...","274":"Boys really do grow up fast."};
